 "heard": "A free game made $9 billion in two years. That's about $12 million a day. That was Fortnite in 2018 and 2019. Court papers from Epic's fight with Apple revealed it. Players buy V-Bucks to spend in its item shop. Today, 40% of that shop money goes into a pot for the people who build its islands. It's shared out by how much people play each island. By May 2026, Creators Islands took 47% of all playing time. Since 2023, Epic has paid creators more than $1 billion. But in March 2026, Epic cut more than 1,000 jobs. Its boss said a Fortnite slump left Epic, spending far more than it made. A week earlier, it had raised the price of V-Bucks, saying Fortnite cost more to run. Even a free game has to pay its bills. And remember...",
